078 #edb/ref 17592186358847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360140 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5ed81ec3-d906-5a86-bc7c-31b1ba6834fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186357803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186359354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360333 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c4f2da6b-5bbf-5958-acfc-6db810c9ab3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186357793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186357793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360439 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9feea77-0770-57d9-9bdc-bf443c95c674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186359542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360451 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fef695bf-af69-5590-8e72-7ce89ea59101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360527 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360527 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94887" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360527 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360527 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\sqrt{t},3t-1⟩$ at the point $t=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360527 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53f0d6f9-0bd0-5fbc-870f-a5ea8fa6cdba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360527 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz),\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨yz,xz,xy⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=2t,y=\\sqrt{t}$ and $z=3t-1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨\\sqrt{t}(3t-1),2t(3t-1),2t\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(3t-1)\\sqrt{t},6{t}^{2}-2t,2t\\sqrt{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨(3t-1)\\sqrt{t},6{t}^{2}-2t,2t\\sqrt{t}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},3⟩ \\\\  & =(3t-1)\\sqrt{t}\\cdot 2+(6{t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+2t\\sqrt{t}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6t\\sqrt{t}-2\\sqrt{t}+\\frac{3{t}^{2}-t}{\\sqrt{t}}+6t\\sqrt{t} \\\\  & =12t\\sqrt{t}-2\\sqrt{t}+\\frac{3{t}^{2}-t}{\\sqrt{t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(1))] & =12(1)\\sqrt{1}-2\\sqrt{1}+\\frac{3(1)^{2}-1}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360528 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360528 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360528 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360528 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)=x{z}^{2}+{y}^{3}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,4,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩$ at the point $t=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "102aa53b-1989-56be-b06a-9a6f6770770c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360528 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{z}^{2}+{y}^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{2}+{y}^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{z}^{2}+{y}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{z}^{2},3{y}^{2},2xz⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,$ $y=4$ and $z=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3})^{2},3(4)^{2},2t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-3,48,2t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-3,48,2t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}}⟩ \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-3)\\cdot 1+48\\cdot 0+2t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}\\cdot \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-3}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-3+0+2{t}^{2} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(2))] & =3(2)^{2}-3 \\\\  & =12-3 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360544 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360544 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360544 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360544 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $r(t)=\\pi t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360544 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4eac0cd5-9d30-54ff-89b8-2cfd1b9003d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360544 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,j \\\\  & =-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\pi t$ and $y={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\pi \\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j)\\cdot (\\pi \\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\pi {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360545 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360545 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360545 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360545 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})$ and $r(t)={t}^{-2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360545 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99c33c9d-4cdd-5e75-a91b-a13201898eee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360545 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2xy}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\frac{2}{y}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={t}^{-2}$ and $y={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{-2}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{{e}^{t}}\\,j \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{-2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =-2{t}^{-3}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j)\\cdot (-2{t}^{-3}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =-2({t}^{2})({t}^{-3})+2{e}^{-t}({e}^{t}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{2}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(t-1)}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360548 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360548 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360548 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360548 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2t\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360548 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a60dcabe-5a9f-584e-9268-2f3213ceda5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360548 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\,i-4{y}^{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $z=2t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,i-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & 